00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:46.440
oh you played in it.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:47.816
That's awesome.

00:04:47.816 --> 00:04:50.900
Cool, it's in every crevice of your crib,

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:52.113
probably in your mouth.

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:56.200
And then you just cry, Erin, you just cry.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.800
- So I'll take that back,
we're not gonna have kids.

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:01.760
I'm fine with just Howard.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:04.190
- All right, switching gears from poo,

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:05.900
you were, no, this is
actually more serious,

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:08.170
and my family's been highly
affected by cervical cancer,

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:10.530
and you were actually
diagnosed in 2016, right?

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:13.360
So, I guess my question
is, you're fine now right?

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:14.193
- Fine right now.

00:05:14.193 --> 00:05:15.130
- And how did you find out?

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:16.733
- Just honestly, thank you,

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:20.430
just from a regular annual exam.

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:22.820
I mean, right before I go to
football season every year,

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:23.930
it's like going back to school

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:25.990
when your mom would like
get your teeth checked,

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:28.480
now it's like go to the
doctor, go to the gyno,

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:31.500
get the extensions done, get
the roots done, all that.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:34.320
And I, literally yeah, week
three of the football season

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:35.560
that year, got a text.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.170
And you know when you
get a text from your gyno

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.910
on a Saturday it's not good.

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:41.000
So, yeah, wheel's went into motion,

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.450
and ended up having two
cervical cancer surgeries.

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:44.980
There was a little bit of a concern

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:46.660
that I was gonna have
to have a hysterectomy,

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:50.460
but I did not have to
have that, thank god.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:51.900
- I had that happen with a friend,

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:55.280
and I always tell all
my friends, I'm like,

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:56.890
get your eggs first before you do it,

00:05:56.890 --> 00:05:58.040
because after radiation, you know.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:00.350
- Oh yeah, and that
was a big thing for us,

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:01.990
like, before we had the second surgery

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:03.040
when the first one didn't work,

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:04.660
there was a big conversation we did.

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:05.620
We've done all that stuff,

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:07.550
but you have to, you have to make sure.

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:08.630
- Some doctors don't mention that

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:09.870
because they're so
concerned about the cancer.

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:11.080
Obviously we're concerned
about the patient,

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:12.899
but that's an important
thing for women and men

00:06:12.899 --> 00:06:14.170
that want children.

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:16.260
- Yeah, and even more
important, I mean again,

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:19.060
there's no symptoms with
cervical cancer, I was fine.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:22.050
And I remember when we first
got the test results back,

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:23.500
I remember telling some of my friends

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:26.320
and they were like, you're
fine, you work out all the time,

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.450
you eat right, you're in great shape,

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:29.633
and I was like, it has
nothing to do with that.

00:06:29.633 --> 00:06:31.631
- That was literally my next point,

00:06:31.631 --> 00:06:33.140
and I was gonna say, you're
like the picture of health,

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:34.220
and it can happen to anyone,

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:35.730
and you really should
get regular checkups.

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:38.170
- And again, because there
aren't any symptoms of it,

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:40.140
and I just found it on an annual exam,

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:42.050
and even worse, not to scare everybody

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:43.740
and get them on Web MD right now,

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:45.458
but I was going every single year.

00:06:45.458 --> 00:06:48.690
So it's not like I was
somebody that missed my annual,

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:50.586
I was going every single year.

00:06:50.586 --> 00:06:52.640
Then I had friends, after I came out

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.090
and I revealed that I had had it,

00:06:54.090 --> 00:06:55.710
said oh my god I haven't
been in three years,

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:57.910
and I'm like, would you, you
need to go to the doctor.

00:06:57.910 --> 00:06:59.845
Like you just have to go and get checked,

00:06:59.845 --> 00:07:02.807
because much like prostate
cancer which my dad had,

00:07:02.807 --> 00:07:05.140
you should not die of cervical cancer.

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:07.230
It's curable and it is detectable,

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:09.260
and you just need to go to the doctor.

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:11.330
- But the reason why
the rate is so alarming

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:12.840
with ovarian and cervical cancer is

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:14.970
because you don't know you have it.

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:16.400
So by the time you know you have it,

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:18.240
you might be at stage four.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:19.760
Yeah, so that's why it's so deadly.

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:22.080
- So after this, call your doctor,

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.190
go get your checkup.

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:25.088
- Get in those stirrups, ladies.

00:07:25.088 --> 00:07:26.720
(applause)

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:29.800
- I mean, I am so
thankful for my oncologist

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:31.940
and everything, and he
is such a wonderful,

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:33.690
good-looking man, and I'm always so sad

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:36.071
that's how I see him every six months.

00:07:36.071 --> 00:07:38.900
Because I do, I have to
go every six months now.

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:40.770
That's my checkup, it is horrible,

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:42.560
and then you go, and they
take your blood pressure,

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:43.780
and they're like your blood pressure's up,

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:45.670
and I'm like, well no crap.

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:47.278
I'm like waiting to get this test done.

00:07:47.278 --> 00:07:50.030
Yeah, and then I leave, and
I got eat a big fat donut,

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:51.740
and I go shopping, I'm like whew!

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:52.640
- You deserve it at that point.

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:54.313
- Yeah, eat a pizza.

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:56.873
- Oh my god, I love pizza.

00:07:56.873 --> 00:07:59.650
So, the new season of Dancing
with the Stars premiered,

